trade|buying-selling-activity|NOUN|buying and selling activity|The activity of buying and selling goods or services, especially between people or places.|hoạt động mua bán; thương mại|Trade between the two ports created work for local families.|Hoạt động buôn bán giữa hai cảng tạo việc làm cho các gia đình địa phương.|Usually uncountable; trade between places concerns commercial activity, not one person's occupation.|trade
trade|do-business|VERB|do business with others|Buy, sell or exchange goods or services as part of a business relationship.|buôn bán; giao dịch thương mại|The farm trades with several restaurants in the region.|Trang trại giao dịch với một số nhà hàng trong vùng.|Intransitive with with for a business partner; this sense is distinct from swapping particular items.|trade
trade|skilled-occupation|NOUN|skilled practical occupation|A type of work that requires practical training and skill.|nghề thủ công hoặc nghề chuyên môn|After school, he trained for a trade in electrical repair.|Sau khi học xong, anh học nghề sửa chữa điện.|Countable; learn a trade refers to an occupation, rather than commerce as an activity.|trade
trade|exchange-items|VERB|exchange items|Give one item and receive another in return, usually without buying or selling them.|trao đổi đồ vật|The children traded stickers during the lunch break.|Bọn trẻ đổi nhãn dán cho nhau trong giờ ăn trưa.|Transitive; trade one thing for another describes an exchange of items, not commercial dealing with a partner.|trade
multiply|arithmetic-product|VERB|calculate a product|Find the result of multiplying one number by another.|nhân trong phép tính|Multiply eight by seven to find the total number of tiles.|Nhân tám với bảy để tìm tổng số viên gạch.|Transitive; multiply one number by another, with the product as the result.|multiply
multiply|increase-or-reproduce|VERB|increase in number|Increase in number, or produce more organisms of the same kind.|tăng lên nhiều lần; sinh sôi|The bacteria multiplied quickly in the warm water.|Vi khuẩn sinh sôi nhanh trong nước ấm.|Often intransitive for an increase or reproduction; do not confuse this with arithmetic multiplication.|multiply
until|endpoint-time-phrase|PREPOSITION|up to a time|Up to and including a particular time or event.|cho đến một mốc thời gian|The repair shop will stay open until six this evening.|Tiệm sửa chữa sẽ mở cửa đến sáu giờ tối nay.|Preposition followed by a time noun phrase; distinguish until a time from until followed by a clause.|until
until|endpoint-clause|CONJUNCTION|up to when something happens|Up to the time when a stated event happens.|cho đến khi một việc xảy ra|We waited until the rain stopped before leaving the station.|Chúng tôi đợi đến khi mưa tạnh rồi mới rời nhà ga.|Conjunction followed by a subject and verb; a present tense clause can refer to a future time.|until
county|administrative-area|NOUN|administrative area|An area used as a unit of local administration in some countries.|hạt; đơn vị hành chính|The county council repaired the footbridge near the village.|Hội đồng hạt sửa cây cầu đi bộ gần ngôi làng.|Countable; the exact level and powers of a county vary by jurisdiction.|county
baby|very-young-child|NOUN|very young child|A very young child who is not yet able to walk or speak well.|em bé; trẻ sơ sinh hoặc trẻ rất nhỏ|The baby slept peacefully while the family prepared dinner.|Em bé ngủ ngon trong lúc gia đình chuẩn bị bữa tối.|Countable; this sense concerns a very young child, not the youngest member of a family of any age.|baby
baby|youngest-family-member|NOUN|youngest family member|The youngest person in a family or group, even when that person is no longer a small child.|em út; người nhỏ tuổi nhất trong gia đình|Although she is thirty, she is still the baby of the family.|Dù đã ba mươi tuổi, cô vẫn là em út trong gia đình.|Often the baby of the family; this figurative use identifies relative age, not infancy.|baby
dictate|determine-requirements|VERB|determine what is required|Set or determine what must happen because of a rule, need or condition.|quy định; chi phối điều cần làm|Safety rules dictate where visitors may stand during the tour.|Quy định an toàn quyết định vị trí khách được đứng trong chuyến tham quan.|A rule, condition or need can dictate a requirement or clause; distinguish this from a person issuing orders.|dictate
dictate|impose-orders|VERB|tell others what to do|Tell someone what they must do or how they must behave, often without allowing choice.|ra lệnh; áp đặt cách hành động|The manager should explain the schedule instead of dictating how every worker must spend the day.|Quản lý nên giải thích lịch làm việc thay vì áp đặt cách mỗi nhân viên phải trải qua cả ngày.|A person dictates what or how someone should act; this sense concerns control over another person's choices.|dictate
dictate|speak-for-transcription|VERB|speak for someone to write down|Say words aloud for another person to record in writing.|đọc cho người khác ghi chép|The director dictated a short letter to her assistant.|Giám đốc đọc một lá thư ngắn cho trợ lý ghi lại.|Transitive; dictate a letter or a letter to somebody describes speaking for transcription, not giving an order.|dictate
tumor|abnormal-tissue-mass|NOUN|abnormal mass of tissue|A mass of abnormal tissue that forms in the body; it may or may not be cancerous.|khối u; khối mô bất thường|The scan showed a small tumor near the lung, but further tests were needed.|Kết quả chụp ghi nhận khối u ở vùng phổi; cần kiểm tra thêm.|Countable; a tumor is not necessarily cancerous; the spelling here follows the selected US source form.|tumor
opposed|disagreeing-with|ADJECTIVE|disagreeing with a proposal|Disagreeing with or against a plan, action or idea.|phản đối; không tán thành|Several residents were opposed to closing the library.|Một số cư dân phản đối việc đóng cửa thư viện.|Use be opposed to followed by a noun or an -ing form; this adjective is not the verb oppose.|opposed
reconstruction|physical-rebuilding|NOUN|rebuilding something physical|The process of building or putting something back together after it has been damaged or destroyed.|sự xây dựng lại; việc tái thiết|The reconstruction of the old bridge took nearly two years.|Việc xây dựng lại cây cầu cũ mất gần hai năm.|Uncountable for the process; this sense rebuilds a physical structure rather than digitally representing it.|reconstruction
reconstruction|recreation-from-evidence|NOUN|representation recreated from evidence|A representation of how something may have looked, made from available evidence.|bản phục dựng; sự tái hiện từ bằng chứng|The museum displayed a digital reconstruction of the temple as it may once have appeared.|Bảo tàng trưng bày bản phục dựng kỹ thuật số về diện mạo ngôi đền trong quá khứ.|Countable; a digital reconstruction represents a possible former appearance without rebuilding the original object.|reconstruction
reconstruction|system-reorganization|NOUN|reorganization of a system|A major change intended to improve the way a system or set of conditions is organized.|sự tái tổ chức; việc cải tổ hệ thống|The report called for a reconstruction of the education system.|Báo cáo kêu gọi tái tổ chức hệ thống giáo dục.|Uncountable; reconstruction of a system changes its organization, rather than rebuilding one structure.|reconstruction
issue|matter-for-attention|NOUN|matter for discussion or concern|A subject or problem that people discuss, consider or need to deal with.|vấn đề; chủ đề cần quan tâm|Housing costs became a central issue at the town meeting.|Chi phí nhà ở trở thành vấn đề trọng tâm tại cuộc họp thị trấn.|Countable; an issue can be a subject or concern and is not necessarily a fault or dispute.|issue
issue|officially-provide|VERB|provide officially|Officially give or make a document, item or statement available to someone.|cấp; phát hành chính thức|The office issued new identification cards to all staff members.|Văn phòng cấp thẻ nhận dạng mới cho toàn thể nhân viên.|Transitive; issue something to someone, especially an official document or item.|issue
issue|periodical-edition|NOUN|single periodical edition|One particular edition of a magazine, journal or newspaper.|số báo; số tạp chí|The latest issue of the journal includes an interview with the researcher.|Số tạp chí mới nhất có một cuộc phỏng vấn nhà nghiên cứu.|Countable; an issue of a magazine refers to one edition, not a subject discussed in it.|issue
thorough|careful-and-complete|ADJECTIVE|careful and complete|Including all important details and done with great care.|kỹ lưỡng; đầy đủ và cẩn thận|A thorough inspection found no damage to the roof.|Một cuộc kiểm tra kỹ lưỡng không phát hiện mái nhà bị hư hại.|Often modifies inspection, check or explanation; describes completeness and care rather than a particular task.|thorough
privatization|government-to-private-ownership|NOUN|transfer to private ownership|The process of transferring a business or service from government ownership to private ownership.|sự tư nhân hóa; chuyển sang sở hữu tư nhân|The debate focused on the privatization of the national railway.|Cuộc tranh luận tập trung vào việc tư nhân hóa ngành đường sắt quốc gia.|Uncountable; privatization names a change in ownership and does not by itself express whether that change is beneficial.|privatization
indoors|inside-building|ADVERB|inside a building|Inside a building rather than outside.|ở trong nhà; trong tòa nhà|The visitors waited indoors until the storm passed.|Khách chờ trong nhà cho đến khi cơn bão đi qua.|Adverb; stay or wait indoors. The adjective before a noun is indoor, which is outside this entry's POS.|indoors
livelihood|means-of-living|NOUN|means of earning a living|The work or source of income that provides what a person needs to live.|kế sinh nhai; sinh kế|Fishing on the lake is the main livelihood for many families nearby.|Đánh cá trên hồ là kế sinh nhai chính của nhiều gia đình sống gần đó.|Countable or uncountable by context; a livelihood is a means of supporting oneself, not every source of income or pastime.|livelihood
neighbour|person-living-nearby|NOUN|person living nearby|A person who lives near you or near a particular place.|hàng xóm; người sống gần|Our neighbour collected the parcel while we were away.|Người hàng xóm nhận giúp bưu kiện khi chúng tôi đi vắng.|Countable; the selected headword uses the British spelling neighbour; neighbor is a US spelling variant in the source data.|neighbour
amuse|entertain-or-make-laugh|VERB|make someone enjoy themselves|Make someone find something entertaining or funny.|làm vui; làm cho thích thú hoặc buồn cười|The musicians amused the children with a playful song.|Các nhạc công làm bọn trẻ thích thú bằng một bài hát vui nhộn.|Transitive; amuse somebody describes the effect on the person, whether through entertainment or humor.|amuse
confess|admit-unwelcome-truth|VERB|admit a troubling truth|Admit that something one has done or believes is true, especially when it is embarrassing or wrong.|thú nhận; thừa nhận điều gây khó xử|After the meeting, Linh confessed that she had forgotten to send the file.|Sau cuộc họp, Linh thú nhận rằng cô đã quên gửi tệp.|Transitive or followed by that; confess to doing something is another common pattern. The source's religious gloss is not covered here.|confess
bonus|extra-reward-money|NOUN|extra payment as a reward|An extra payment given in addition to a person's usual pay, often as a reward.|tiền thưởng; khoản trả thêm|The team received a year-end bonus for completing the project.|Nhóm nhận được tiền thưởng cuối năm vì đã hoàn thành dự án.|Countable; a bonus paid with or in addition to salary is a monetary reward, not a general non-cash benefit.|bonus
bonus|additional-benefit|NOUN|additional advantage|An extra benefit or pleasing feature in addition to what was expected.|lợi ích thêm; điểm cộng|A free breakfast was an added bonus of staying at the small hotel.|Bữa sáng miễn phí là một lợi ích thêm khi nghỉ tại khách sạn nhỏ.|Often an added bonus; this is an extra benefit rather than a payment of money.|bonus
downward|towards-lower-level|ADJECTIVE|moving toward a lower level|Moving or pointing toward a lower position or value.|hướng xuống; giảm dần|The report showed a downward trend in monthly complaints.|Báo cáo cho thấy số khiếu nại hằng tháng có xu hướng giảm.|Before a noun such as trend or movement; this entry follows the frozen adjective POS and covers a direction toward a lower level.|downward
institutional|organization-related|ADJECTIVE|related to an organization|Connected with a large or established organization.|thuộc tổ chức; liên quan đến cơ quan|Institutional investors discussed the risks at the annual meeting.|Các nhà đầu tư tổ chức thảo luận về rủi ro tại cuộc họp thường niên.|Before a noun; institutional investors are investors that are organizations rather than individuals.|institutional
institutional|embedded-in-systems|ADJECTIVE|embedded in a system's structures|Part of the established structures, rules or practices of a society or organization.|mang tính thể chế; nằm trong cơ cấu và quy tắc hệ thống|The researchers studied institutional inequality across several regions.|Các nhà nghiên cứu tìm hiểu bất bình đẳng mang tính thể chế ở một số khu vực.|Before a noun; institutional inequality concerns patterns within systems, distinct from an investor's organizational status.|institutional
